      },
      {
        "declared_pt": 43.2,
        "fill": false,
        "h": 71.9921875,
        "left": 71.9921875,
        "path": "/slide[3]/shape[@id=2]",
        "text": "Commercial commentary",
        "top": 53.984375,
        "w": 1451.9921875
      },
      {
        "declared_pt": 64.8,
        "fill": false,
        "h": 557.08984375,
        "left": 71.9921875,
        "path": "/slide[3]/shape[@id=3]",
        "text": "Net revenue closed the quarter at 98.9B MMK, 12.4% ahead of the same quarter last year and 4.1% ahead of plan, with the beat concentrated in the modern trade channel where average basket size rose from 11,332 to 11,488 MMK. In-store remains the volume engine at 376.2B MMK across the trailing twelve months, but delivery grew fastest at 21.8% year on year and is now within 6% of in-store on a per-order margin basis, which is the first quarter that has been true. Promotional depth was the single largest swing factor: the share of net revenue transacted under an active promotion fell from 34.6% to 28.9%, and roughly two thirds of the gross margin improvement traces back to that reduction rather than to price or to mix. Yangon contributed 61% of the increase, Mandalay 18%, and the remaining branches split the balance with no single outlet moving the total by more than 40 basis points. Inventory turns improved from 6.2 to 6.9 while out-of-stock incidents on the top 200 SKUs fell by a third, so the revenue gain was not bought with working capital. The two watch items into next quarter are the loyalty cohort, where redemption rate has drifted down for three consecutive months, and the supplier concentration in chilled goods, where a single vendor now accounts for 41% of category cost of goods sold.",
        "top": 210,
        "w": 887.98828125
      },
      {
        "declared_pt": 108,
        "fill": true,
        "h": 180,
        "left": 71.9921875,
        "path": "/slide[3]/shape[@id=4]",
