      },
      {
        "declared_pt": 20.16,
        "fill": false,
        "h": 33.59375,
        "left": 95.99609375,
        "path": "/slide[4]/shape[@id=29]",
        "text": "Store-Level Commentary",
        "top": 626.38671875,
        "w": 1415.99609375
      },
      {
        "declared_pt": 97.2,
        "fill": false,
        "h": 227.96875,
        "left": 95.99609375,
        "path": "/slide[4]/shape[@id=30]",
        "text": "Ocean hypermarkets in Yangon still occupy the top five slots by absolute revenue, confirming the hypermarket estate as the volume backbone. Three of those five grew\u2014Yangon 74, 72, and 70\u2014but Yangon 73 is a clear outlier, down 18.9% year on year while remaining the fourth-largest store. That single-site swing is large enough to matter at banner level and deserves a dedicated operational review (assortment, local competition, disruption, or renovation effects). Below the Ocean tier, several City Mart supermarkets posted standout growth: Yangon 63 (+32%), Yangon 46 (+25%), and Yangon 59 (+20%) show the supermarket format can still take share when execution is right. Outside Lower Myanmar, Mandalay 48 grew 14% while Monywa 51 slipped 5%. Concentration risk remains high: eight of the top ten stores sit in Yangon / Lower Myanmar.",
        "top": 662.3828125,
        "w": 1415.99609375
      },
