        "h": 227.96875,
        "left": 90,
        "path": "/slide[5]/shape[@id=41]",
        "text": "Category mix in Q4 remains anchored in Fresh and Health. Vitamins & Supplements alone contribute about 11% of net sales and held steady year on year\u2014an important stabilizer when perishable categories are soft. Fresh as a department is still ~29% of revenue but is the largest absolute drag (\u22124.3% YoY), with Dairy & Eggs and Seafood the main pressure points inside that franchise. Grocery\u2019s Canned & Packaged decline (\u22128.3%) echoes a weaker center-store basket. Personal Care is mixed: Skin Care and Hair Care declined, while Bath & Body grew nearly 5%. Bakery\u2019s 8% decline aligns with the softer Seasons Bakery banner print. For the board, the strategic read is twofold: defend Fresh availability and perceived quality to stop further share leakage, and keep leaning into stable high-ticket Health and growing personal-care adjacencies that are already proving resilient.",
